+## Changed
+
+- Added `crates/apps/cli/src/lib.rs` with `CliResult`, `features()` and `run_cli`. The registry is `plan`, `approve`, `archive`, `land`, `inbox`, `report`; help is built only from each feature's `commands()`; dispatch calls the first feature that lists the name and maps `Output`/`FeatureError` to stdout/stderr and code 0/1.
+- Replaced the empty `crates/apps/cli/src/main.rs` with the entry point: it reads the current directory and UTF-8 arguments, calls `run_cli`, writes both streams, and exits with the result code. Unreadable directories and non-UTF-8 arguments print one stderr line and exit 1.
+- Added `crates/apps/cli/tests/run_cli.rs` for registry order, crate ownership, both help forms, help covering every registered command, unknown commands, and first-feature-wins.
+- Added `crates/apps/cli/tests/binary.rs` for `inbox`, `queue` and `query SELECT 1 AS one` through the built binary against fresh fixture copies, a feature error, unknown command exit code, and the two entry-point input errors.
+- Added `crates/apps/cli/tests/support/mod.rs` with the feature double, call counters and fixture copy helper.
+- Added the fixture project under `crates/apps/cli/tests/fixtures/project/` with `openspec/queue.md` and change `001-alpha` (`brief.md`, `proposal.md`).
+- `cargo test -p osq-cli` passes (11 tests). `cargo fmt --all` was run. `cargo mutants -p osq-cli -f crates/apps/cli/src/lib.rs -f crates/apps/cli/src/main.rs` reported 28 caught, 7 unviable, 0 missed.
+
+## Deviated
+
+- Added two extra binary tests beyond the listed scenarios, for non-UTF-8 arguments and an unreadable current directory, because "CLI entry point" requires those errors and the mutation gate covers `main.rs`. Both are tagged `Covers: rust-cli/binary-exit-code`.
+
+## Missing context
+
+- The proposal's verify cannot pass with `OSQ_CHANGE` set to this change. `change_link_gates` merges ADDED/MODIFIED `Code ownership` deltas but ignores REMOVED ones, so the living `rust-workspace` ownership of `crates/apps/cli/**` remains while the `rust-cli` delta adds the same globs. The corpus test then reports every new `crates/apps/cli` file as owned by both capabilities. Without `OSQ_CHANGE`, the same corpus test reports the new `rust-cli` tags as not living. The planner needs to decide how this change removes `rust-workspace`'s ownership during its own run, or add a linter change that applies REMOVED `Code ownership` requirements.
+
+## Outside scope
+
+- `crates/kernel/linter`'s `merge_ownership` ignores `delta.removed`, so a change that removes a capability's only `Code ownership` requirement overlaps with the capability that takes over its files. I left it unchanged.
+- The same linter gap means `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` fails in `link_gates_corpus` with OSQ_CHANGE set: `crates/apps/cli/src/lib.rs`, `main.rs`, `tests/binary.rs`, `tests/run_cli.rs` and `tests/support/mod.rs` are reported as owned by `rust-cli, rust-workspace`.
+
+## Blocked
+
+- Completion needs either a linter change so `change_link_gates` drops the ownership of a capability whose delta REMOVES its `Code ownership` requirement, or a planner revision of this change's rust-workspace delta that avoids the overlap during the change's own run. The CLI crate itself is implemented and its task verify passes.
+
+## Next
+
+- Once ownership is resolved, rerun `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` with `OSQ_CHANGE` pointing at this change; no `crates/apps/cli` work remains.
+
+Touched: crates/apps/cli/src/lib.rs, crates/apps/cli/src/main.rs, crates/apps/cli/tests/run_cli.rs, crates/apps/cli/tests/binary.rs, crates/apps/cli/tests/support/mod.rs, crates/apps/cli/tests/fixtures/project/openspec/queue.md, crates/apps/cli/tests/fixtures/project/openspec/changes/001-alpha/brief.md, crates/apps/cli/tests/fixtures/project/openspec/changes/001-alpha/proposal.md
